    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0737" n="717" xml:id="pg717"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 28, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> On the 31st ultimo I had the honor to bring
                    to your notice the ease of Mr. Charles A. Russell, of the British sloop Racer,
                    captured off Bull’s bay, and to request that an investigation of the matter
                    might be made; and on the 3d instant you informed me that a copy of my note had
                    been transmitted to the Navy Department.</p>
                <p>I shall be glad to learn how this affair now stands.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi>,<hi rendition="#italic">
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
